Hey [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] , thanks for getting back timely with an extensive overview.

To answer your questions:

* However, I note your comment “_I am still exploring if I can outsource sending (for instance by the postal office), what would we need to set up in order to comply? Would it be different if we would directly link to a form owned by the postal office, where the personal details are collected for this specific purpose?_” - can you provide more context on what you mean by this? - {color:#bf2600}Given the complications toward data processing and limited time, we will not consider this approach any longer. Taking this as a learning for future engagement initiatives.{color}
* *How do we know which drivers to send these comms to*? Are we sending it to all NL drivers (regardless of background) who have been active in the last 90 days? Or are we only sending it to drivers who we know are Muslim? - {color:#bf2600}We’ve expanded the targeting to include as many partners as possible, without excluding anyone based on religion. All drivers active in the last 180 days are included. Those who find this irrelevant are unlikely to engage or sign up. The sign-up process ensures drivers self-select, rather than us making the choice for them.{color}

Thank you for consulting me on this topic. I think we now have enough input to go on with the approach as agreed on. Let me know if you think it’s good to go too!

