Hey [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] , my comments from a Privacy POV:

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Re booking data*
{panel}

{quote}_“your interpretation of the data-sharing obligations under the regulations is overly restrictive and does not reflect the full scope of the applicable legal framework. Your reference to Part IX, Section 65.6(ii) of the Regulations is noted, however, the obligation to provide "booking data" cannot be interpreted in isolation. Regulation 36 of S.L. 499.68 unequivocally states that operators must install_ *_tracking_* *_devices_* _on vehicles and ensure that all recorded data is made available to the Authority upon request. This requirement establishes that data-sharing obligations extend beyond booking-related information and include operational and tracking data relevant to enforcement and regulatory compliance.”_{quote}

* What tracking devices are they referencing [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] ? Do we have them? If we use the app as a tracker, what are we supposed to track?
* I think this bit is weak - they still didn’t mention what we need to share under law. So, unless we know what these tracking devices are supposed to track, I can’t tell if we have a direct legal obligation to share data. Now, it seems like they want us to share all data they might need.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Re data that we need to share / the purpose of this data*
{panel}

{quote}_The additional data requested, such as driver session times, vehicle specifications, and driver identifiers, is crucial for Transport Malta to ensure_ *_compliance with regulatory requirements_*_. These obligations, which are enshrined in law, necessitate the provision of the full dataset requested by the Authority. The selective disclosure of only certain categories of information undermines regulatory oversight and is not in line with the intent or spirit of S.L. 499.68._{quote}

* I think we still have some space here, as while they’re mentioning that we’re aiming to do selective disclosure, we are doing this for the purpose of ensuring that we don’t overshare data.
* This will depend on the answer to my question above re tracking devices, and if we know what they’re supposed to track.
* Until that is clear, we can presume that don’t know what they need and are they’re trying to hide the unclarity on their end by pushing us aggressively
* Also, it is unclear to me why having 3 identifiers instead of one is “crucial” for them to ensure compliance

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Re legal basis of sharing data*
{panel}

{quote}_While Bolt is correct in highlighting its obligations under GDPR, it is important to note that the sharing of requested data with a regulatory authority falls under the_ *_lawful basis of public interest and legal obligation_* _as defined under Article 6(1)(c) and (e) of the GDPR. The processing and sharing of such data are necessary for the execution of Transport Malta's statutory functions and_ *_do not require a separate data-sharing agreement or an MoU_* _to be enforceable._{quote}

* This point isn’t invalid. We can agree to move forward without MoU, but the main purpose for MoU is to control what we’re sharing, and to give some structure to it. MoU will help us put a rational setup in place, where TM tells us what they need, and what we need to share
* Otherwise, we can’t guarantee that they won’t be coming in 1 month saying that even more data is booking data and they need more
* So, we’re using MoU as a tool to structure data sharing, and making sure it’s all set in paper, and not by a gentleman’s agreement



{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Re data minimization and MoU*
{panel}

{quote}_The principle of data minimisation under GDPR does not preclude the sharing of necessary operational data when required by law. In this regard, the proposed MoU is not a prerequisite for compliance and does not override Bolt's direct obligations under Maltese legislation._{quote}

* We do have obligations, I agree. But we need to make sure that those obligations are clear. For now, until we have clarity on what we are required to share by law, or what they really need, we are within our rights to bring out the “data minimization principle” card and reduce the scope of data shared.



----

