If so, I have reviewed the agreements and have no substantive comments on these. My updated advice is therefore as follows:

{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}
We are ok with *green-lighting* this feature, *_provided that_*:

* We are keeping a *paper trail* of why a particular document was accepted;
* The automated process does not significantly increase the chance of *fraudulent documents* being accepted;
* We are providing drivers with a high-level *explanation of why a document is rejected* (if we are not already doing so); 
* In relation to any use of machine learning models to extract data from driver documents, the preference would always be to use in-house services. However, where we need to leverage external services (like ChatGPT), this is ok as long as we do so in a sensible and limited way. In particular, we should not allow ChatGPT to use driver data to train its models, and we should be confident that any driver data we are putting through ChatGPT is accurate; and
* We are *NOT* doing any biometric processing in this context ([~accountid:712020:666b819e-7279-4447-91d0-83971e72f35a] please confirm).
